      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "Acetaldehyde",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "Formaldehyde",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "Benzaldehyde",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "Trimethylacetaldehyde",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Cannizzaro reaction is given by aldehydes which do not have an $\\alpha$-hydrogen. Acetaldehyde ($\\mathrm{CH_3CHO}$) has three $\\alpha$-hydrogens, so it undergoes aldol condensation instead of Cannizzaro reaction under basic conditions."
    },
    {
      "ref": "CHEM-ALD-002",
      "subtopic": "chemical-properties",
      "type": "single_correct",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "expected_time_sec": 95,
      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The reaction of benzaldehyde with concentrated $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ solution followed by acidification yields:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "Benzyl alcohol and benzoic acid",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "Benzophenone and sodium benzoate",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "Benzyl alcohol and phenol",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "Benzoic acid and sodium benzoate",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Benzaldehyde does not contain any $\\alpha$-hydrogen. Thus, on treatment with concentrated alkali, it undergoes Cannizzaro reaction (disproportionation) to yield benzyl alcohol (reduced product) and sodium benzoate. Acidification converts the sodium salt to benzoic acid."
